# DISTANCES: the triangle inequality for lengths, from the one for their cosh's.
#
# order.tree proves cosh d(a, c) <= cosh d(a, b) cosh d(b, c) + sinh d(a, b) sinh d(b, c), the right side being
# cosh (d(a, b) + d(b, c)) by the addition formula (integral/exponential, integral/hyperbolic-functions). What turns
# that into d(a, c) <= d(a, b) + d(b, c) is that cosh is STRICTLY INCREASING on [0, oo):
#
#   THE STEP             cosh(x + w) - cosh x = cosh x (cosh w - 1) + sinh x sinh w, which is positive for x >= 0 and
#                        w > 0, as cosh w - 1 >= w^2 / 4 > 0 on (0, 1] (from the exponential's bounds) and cosh x >= 1,
#                        sinh x, sinh w >= 0;
#   THE INEQUALITY       so a distance past the sum would have a cosh past the sum's cosh, which order.tree refuses.
#
# Every certificate is the product prover's, replayed (check/product.ts), over an ordered field.


# THE STEP: with the addition formula cs = cx cw + sx sw, cw > 1, cx >= 1 and sx, sw >= 0, cs > cx.
rule cosh-steps-up
  mark cx, like integer
  mark sx, like integer
  mark cw, like integer
  mark sw, like integer
  mark cs, like integer
  have the-addition-formula
    call is-equal
      read cs
      call add
        call multiply
          read cx
          read cw
        call multiply
          read sx
          read sw
  have cw-is-past-one
    call is-above
      read cw
      code 1
  have cx-is-at-least-one
    call is-minimum
      read cx
      code 1
  have the-sinhs-are-not-negative
    meet and
      call is-minimum
        read sx
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        read sw
        code 0
  show hold
    call is-above
      read cs
      read cx


# cosh = (E + 1/E) / 2 with E between its second- and third-order parts on [0, 1] (integral/hyperbolic-functions):
# 2 cosh w - 2 >= w^2 / 2, as (E - 1)^2 >= (w + w^2 / 2)^2 exceeds E w^2 / 2.
rule cosh-is-a-quarter-square-past-one
  mark w, like integer
  mark ee, like integer
  mark rr, like integer
  have w-is-in-the-unit-interval
    meet and
      call is-minimum
        read w
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        read w
        code 1
  have e-is-above-its-second-order-part
    call is-minimum
      call subtract
        call multiply
          code 2
          read ee
        call add
          call add
            code 2
            call multiply
              code 2
              read w
          call multiply
            read w
            read w
      code 0
  have e-is-below-its-third-order-bound
    call is-maximum
      call subtract
        call multiply
          code 6
          read ee
        call add
          call add
            code 6
            call multiply
              code 6
              read w
          call multiply
            call multiply
              code 3
              read w
            read w
      call multiply
        call multiply
          call multiply
            code 2
            read w
          read w
        read w
  have rr-is-its-reciprocal
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        read ee
        read rr
      code 1
  have rr-is-positive
    call is-above
      read rr
      code 0
  show hold
    call is-minimum
      call multiply
        code 2
        call subtract
          call add
            read ee
            read rr
          code 2
      call multiply
        read w
        read w


# so cosh w > 1 for w > 0.
rule cosh-is-past-one-off-zero
  mark w, like integer
  mark cw, like integer
  have cosh-near-zero
    call is-minimum
      call multiply
        code 4
        call subtract
          read cw
          code 1
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
  have w-is-positive
    call is-above
      read w
      code 0
  show hold
    call is-above
      read cw
      code 1


# THE INEQUALITY: d(a, c) = dac and s = d(a, b) + d(b, c). cosh (ch) is strictly increasing, so x <= y or
# ch(x) > ch(y), and order.tree gives ch(dac) <= ch(s), so dac <= s.
rule the-triangle-inequality-for-distances
  mark ch
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark dac, like integer
  mark s, like integer
  have cosh-is-increasing
    mark x, like integer
    mark y, like integer
    meet or
      call is-maximum
        read x
        read y
      call is-above
        call ch
          read x
        call ch
          read y
  have the-cosh-form
    call is-maximum
      call ch
        read dac
      call ch
        read s
  show hold
    call is-maximum
      read dac
      read s
